# Patch / install Architect Library (Cursor — global readiness default)

**Shared contract:** [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md) — install trigger phrases, editor scope, anti-patterns.

**Editor scope:** You are in **Cursor**. Install to **Cursor paths only** — do not write `~/.copilot/` or `~/.claude/` unless the user explicitly asks for all editors.

When the user asks to **install library**, **install the library**, **patch library**, **refresh library**, **update library**, **install skills and agents**, **sync library**, **update architect library** — or **patch**, **upgrade**, **install**, or **refresh** skills, agents, or Cursor user-global rules — or you finish adding/changing `skills/`, `agents/`, or `user-rules/` in this repo — **run the Cursor readiness install yourself**.

Default means **runtimes + skills + agents + Cursor user-global rules** for Cursor only. Do **not** ask which editor, scope, library subset, or runtime set to install for those trigger phrases.

```bash
bash scripts/install_deps.sh
bash scripts/install_deps.sh office-system
bash scripts/install_library.sh all cursor
```

(`install_deps.sh` includes Node/npm + global `docx`/`pptxgenjs` via `install_node.sh`; re-run `bash scripts/install_deps.sh node` if that step warned.)

If a runtime command fails because of missing permissions, sudo, network, or npm, report the exact failing command and error. Run `bash scripts/runtime_readiness.sh` — skills/agents still install; Word may work via python-docx; new PPT decks need pptxgenjs or a template. Do not claim full artifact readiness until runtimes succeed or you state partial capability per [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md) matrix.

Use partial installs **only** when the user explicitly asks:

- Skills only: `bash scripts/install_library.sh skills cursor`
- Agents only: `bash scripts/install_library.sh agents cursor`
- Cursor user-global rules only: `bash scripts/install_library.sh rules cursor`
- All editors (Cursor + Copilot + Claude): `bash scripts/install_library.sh` — **only** when user asks

**Source of truth:**

- Skills: `<repo>/skills/<name>/`
- Agents: `<repo>/agents/<name>/` (assembled to a single `.md` at install)
- Cursor user-global rules: `<repo>/user-rules/cursor/<name>.mdc`

**Cursor global install targets:**

| Library | Path |
|---------|------|
| Skills | `~/.cursor/skills/<name>/` |
| Agents | `~/.cursor/agents/<name>.md` |
| User-global rules | `~/.cursor/rules/<name>.mdc` |

Use **per-project** `.cursor/skills/` only if the user explicitly wants project-local install (`install_library.sh all cursor project`). Project-scope also copies bundled user-global rules into `<cwd>/.cursor/rules/` without wiping other `.mdc` files — **except** when cwd is this clone (`architect-library`) **or any subdirectory of it**; then rules install is skipped so maintainer `.cursor/rules/` is not overwritten.

Do **not** copy skills into `<repo>/.cursor/skills/`, agents into `<repo>/.cursor/agents/`, or `user-rules/` into `<repo>/.cursor/rules/` — that duplicates source and breaks the install model. One protocol only: edit `user-rules/cursor/`; the host file is an install copy.

## Bundles (in `scripts/install_library.sh`)

```
SKILL_BUNDLE="excalidraw-diagram word-document powerpoint-presentation spreadsheet-document pdf-document verification-before-completion newagentlink api-and-interface-design deprecation-and-migration github-markdown terraform-commit-review terraform-apply-assistance security-audit _shared"
EDITOR_VARIANT_SKILLS="mcp-tool-rules context7-docs notion-mcp-ops"
AGENT_BUNDLE="code-review security-auditor"
CURSOR_RULE_BUNDLE="review-handoff-reconciliation"
LEGACY_SKILLS="docx pptx xlsx pdf terraform-apply-fix-review mcp-tool-rules-copilot handoff"
LEGACY_CURSOR_RULES="code-review-handoff"
```

- **New** skill, agent, or Cursor user-global rule → add to the matching bundle and install target.
- **Existing** entry → **replace** whole folder/file (`rm -rf` then fresh copy/assemble; rules: `rm` then copy the `.mdc`).

## Patch procedure (Cursor)

From the repository root:

```bash
REPO=/path/to/architect-library
cd "$REPO"
bash scripts/install_deps.sh
bash scripts/install_deps.sh office-system
bash scripts/install_library.sh all cursor
```

## Verify (Cursor)

```bash
test -f ~/.cursor/skills/_shared/office-tools/office_tools.py
test -f ~/.cursor/skills/word-document/SKILL.md
test -f ~/.cursor/skills/verification-before-completion/SKILL.md
test -f ~/.cursor/skills/newagentlink/SKILL.md
grep -q 'disable-model-invocation: true' ~/.cursor/skills/newagentlink/SKILL.md
test ! -d ~/.cursor/skills/handoff
test ! -f ~/.cursor/commands/handoff.md
test -f ~/.cursor/commands/newagentlink.md
cmp -s skills/newagentlink/cursor.command.md ~/.cursor/commands/newagentlink.md
test -f ~/.cursor/skills/api-and-interface-design/SKILL.md
test -f ~/.cursor/skills/deprecation-and-migration/SKILL.md
test -f ~/.cursor/skills/security-audit/SKILL.md
test -f ~/.cursor/agents/code-review.md
test -f ~/.cursor/agents/security-auditor.md
grep -q 'readonly: true' ~/.cursor/agents/code-review.md
grep -q 'readonly: true' ~/.cursor/agents/security-auditor.md
test -f ~/.cursor/rules/review-handoff-reconciliation.mdc
grep -q 'alwaysApply: true' ~/.cursor/rules/review-handoff-reconciliation.mdc
test ! -f ~/.cursor/rules/code-review-handoff.mdc
cmp -s user-rules/cursor/review-handoff-reconciliation.mdc ~/.cursor/rules/review-handoff-reconciliation.mdc
cd skills/_shared/office-tools && uv run python3 office_tools.py --help >/dev/null
command -v soffice >/dev/null
command -v pdftoppm >/dev/null
source scripts/architect_env.sh
command -v npm >/dev/null && echo "OK: npm CLI" || echo "WARN: npm CLI missing"
test -d ~/.npm-global/lib/node_modules/docx && test -d ~/.npm-global/lib/node_modules/pptxgenjs && echo "OK: docx/pptxgenjs on disk"
cd skills/_shared/office-tools && uv run python3 -c "import docx" && echo "OK: python-docx"
bash scripts/runtime_readiness.sh
```

The install script runs skill/agent/rule checks automatically when `EDITOR=cursor`. npm and python-docx are optional for library copy; see `runtime_readiness.sh` for artifact capability.

## After patching

1. Tell the user skills, agents, Cursor user-global rules, and runtimes were updated for Cursor.
2. Ask them to **open a new agent chat** (or reload the window) so skill descriptions, agents, and user-global rules reload.
3. If any runtime command failed, say readiness is incomplete and include the failing command.

Full paths, Copilot/Claude variants, and mistakes to avoid: [docs/AGENT-SKILL-INSTALL.md](docs/AGENT-SKILL-INSTALL.md).
